.Dd July 12, 2026
.Dt MESHCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm meshctl
.Nd control the meshd Bluetooth Mesh daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Ar command Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Fl i
.Nm
.Cm help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is the command-line client for
.Xr meshd 8 ,
the Bluetooth Mesh node and network-manager daemon.
It connects to the daemon's line-oriented control socket, sends a single
command (one-shot mode) or a stream of commands (interactive mode), prints each
reply and exits non-zero when the daemon answers
.Ql ERR .
.Pp
.Nm
carries no mesh logic of its own: the daemon owns the node, the created
network, the roster and DevKey store, and the Configuration Client.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl s Ar socket
Connect to
.Ar socket
instead of the default
.Pa /var/run/meshd.sock .
.It Fl i
Interactive mode: read commands from standard input, one per line, until
.Ql quit ,
.Ql exit
or end-of-file.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss Node and network
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm status
Show the node address, provisioning state, sequence number, IV Index and
counters.
.It Cm models
Show every SIG model registered in the local Composition Data together with
the number of AppKey bindings and subscriptions and whether it has a
publication.  This view never exposes NetKeys, AppKeys or Device Keys.
.It Cm create-network
Mint a fresh network (primary NetKey and AppKey, IV Index 0) with this node as
the Provisioner, and begin the manager roster.
.It Cm list-nodes
List the network roster (each node's primary address and element count).
.It Cm provision-scan Oo Cm on | Cm off | Cm list Oc
Control unprovisioned-device discovery: enable
.Pq Cm on , the default with no argument
or disable
.Pq Cm off
parsing of received Unprovisioned Device Beacons, or
.Pq Cm list
report the discovered device UUIDs.
.It Cm provision Ar uuid-hex32 Op Ar elements
Provision a remote device (identified by its 16-octet device UUID) over the air
into the created network, allocating it a unicast address block.
.It Cm provision-gatt Ar addr uuid-hex32 Op Ar elements
Provision an already-connected unprovisioned device through its Mesh
Provisioning Service.  The daemon discovers service UUID 0x1827, writes Data In
UUID 0x2ADB, subscribes to Data Out UUID 0x2ADC, and applies Proxy-PDU SAR at
the negotiated ATT value limit.
.It Cm provision-status
Poll and, when the handshake completes, commit an in-flight over-the-air
provisioning, recording the node and its DevKey.
.It Cm provision-local Ar addr Ar iv
Self-provision this node without an over-the-air exchange.
.It Cm key-refresh Ar sub-verb
Operate Key Refresh on the primary subnet.
.It Cm reset
Clear this node's provisioning.
.El
.Ss Configuration Client
Each
.Cm cfg
sub-verb builds the matching Configuration message, seals it under the target
node's DevKey, sends it to the node's primary element and surfaces the returned
Configuration Status.
.Ar dst
is the target node's unicast address.
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm cfg comp-get Ar dst Op Ar page
Composition Data Get.
.It Cm cfg appkey-add Ar dst
Bind the manager's primary AppKey to the node.
.It Cm cfg model-bind Ar dst Ar elem Ar model Op Ar company
Bind the primary AppKey to a model.
.It Cm cfg sub-add Ar dst Ar elem Ar group Ar model Op Ar company
Subscribe a model to a group address.
.It Cm cfg pub-set Ar dst Ar elem Ar pubaddr Ar ttl Ar period Ar rtx Ar model Op Ar company
Set a model's publication.
.It Cm cfg netkey-add Ar dst Ar netidx Ar key-hex32
Add a subnet NetKey to the node;
.Cm cfg netkey-delete Ar dst Ar netidx
removes it.
.It Cm cfg relay Ar dst Op Ar relay retransmit
Get or set the node's Relay state.
.It Cm cfg beacon | gatt-proxy | friend | ttl Ar dst Op Ar state
Get or set a node-wide state.
.It Cm cfg nettransmit Ar dst Op Ar count intervalsteps
Get or set the Network Transmit state.
.It Cm cfg node-identity-get | node-identity-set Ar dst Ar netidx Op Ar identity
Get or set per-subnet Node Identity.
.It Cm cfg lpn-polltimeout-get Ar dst Ar lpn-addr
Query a Friend's PollTimeout for a Low Power Node.
.It Cm cfg hb-pub-set | hb-sub-set Ar dst Ar ...
Configure Heartbeat publication / subscription.
.It Cm cfg sar-tx-get | sar-rx-get Ar dst
Read the node's SAR Transmitter / Receiver state.
.It Cm cfg sar-tx-set Ar dst Ar segint ucount unoprog uintstep uintinc mcount mintstep
Set the SAR Transmitter state (seven 4-bit fields).
.It Cm cfg sar-rx-set Ar dst Ar segthresh ackdelayinc discard rxintstep ackretrans
Set the SAR Receiver state.
.It Cm cfg priv-beacon-get Ar dst
Read the node's Private Beacon state.
.It Cm cfg priv-beacon-set Ar dst Ar 0 Ns | Ns Ar 1 Op Ar random-update-steps
Set the node's Private Beacon state.
.It Cm cfg priv-gatt-proxy Ar dst Op Ar value
Read or set the node's Private GATT Proxy state.
.It Cm cfg od-priv-proxy Ar dst Op Ar value
Read or set the node's On-Demand Private Proxy state.
.It Cm cfg priv-node-identity-get | priv-node-identity-set Ar dst Ar netidx Op Ar identity
Read or set the node's Private Node Identity for a subnet.
.It Cm cfg lcd-get Ar dst Ar page Ar offset
Large Composition Data Get.
.It Cm cfg node-reset Ar dst
Remove the node from the network.
.El
.Pp
Local Lighting operators include
.Cm lightness-state ,
.Cm lightness-default ,
.Cm lightness-range ,
.Cm ctl-state ,
.Cm ctl-range ,
.Cm hsl-state ,
.Cm hsl-range ,
.Cm xyl-state ,
.Cm xyl-range ,
.Cm lc-mode ,
.Cm lc-om ,
.Cm lc-light-onoff ,
and
.Cm lc-property .
.Cm lc-property
takes a 16-bit property ID and a one- to four-octet hex value.
.Ss Directed Forwarding
The
.Cm df
verbs drive a provisioned node's Directed Forwarding Configuration Server
(sealed under that node's DevKey, over the same path as
.Cm cfg ) ,
plus the local Path Origin path-discovery FSM.
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm df get Ar dst Op Ar netidx
Directed Control Get.
.It Cm df set Ar dst Cm on Ns | Ns Cm off Op Ar netidx
Directed Control Set (turns directed forwarding and directed relay on/off).
.It Cm df control-set Ar dst Ar netidx Ar fwd Ar relay Ar proxy Ar proxydef Ar friend
Directed Control Set with all five flags.
.It Cm df metric-get | metric-set Ar dst Ar ...
Path Metric Get/Set
.Pf ( Cm metric-set Ar dst Ar type Ar lifetime Op Ar netidx ) .
.It Cm df lanes-get | lanes-set Ar dst Ar ...
Directed Wanted Lanes Get/Set.
.It Cm df two-way-get | two-way-set Ar dst Ar ...
Two Way Path Get/Set.
.It Cm df echo-get | echo-set Ar dst Ar ...
Path Echo Interval Get/Set
.Pf ( Cm echo-set Ar dst Ar unicast Ar multicast Op Ar netidx ) .
.It Cm df net-transmit-get | net-transmit-set Ar dst Ar ...
Directed Network Transmit Get/Set
.Pf ( Cm net-transmit-set Ar dst Ar count Ar steps ) .
.It Cm df relay-retransmit-get | relay-retransmit-set Ar dst Ar ...
Directed Relay Retransmit Get/Set.
.It Cm df discover Ar target
Start a local Path Origin path discovery toward
.Ar target .
.It Cm df discover-status
Show the local path-discovery FSM state.
.El
.Ss Remote Provisioning
The
.Cm remote-prov
verbs drive the Remote Provisioning Client toward a provisioned Remote
Provisioning Server node (the RPR models operate under that node's DevKey).
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm remote-prov caps Ar dst
Remote Provisioning Scan Capabilities Get.
.It Cm remote-prov scan Ar dst Op Ar uuid-hex32 Op Ar limit Ar timeout
Remote Provisioning Scan Start (a device UUID targets a single device).
.It Cm remote-prov scan-get | scan-stop Ar dst
Remote Provisioning Scan Get / Scan Stop.
.It Cm remote-prov link-get Ar dst
Remote Provisioning Link Get.
.It Cm remote-prov link-open Ar dst Ar uuid-hex32 Op Ar timeout
Open a PB-Remote provisioning link toward the device
.Ar uuid-hex32
through the server.
.It Cm remote-prov provision Ar dst Ar uuid-hex32 Op Ar timeout
Alias for
.Cm link-open .
.It Cm remote-prov link-close Ar dst Op Ar reason
Remote Provisioning Link Close.
.It Cm remote-prov status
Show the Remote Provisioning client scan/link FSM state.
.El
.Ss Application sockets
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Cm app-register Ar element Ar model Op Ar vendor
Register an application-owned model on this socket.
.It Cm app-events Op Ar max
Drain this socket's queued inbound Access events.
.It Cm app-watch Ar element Ar model Op Ar vendor
Register an application-owned model and keep the connection open, printing the
initial daemon reply and subsequent asynchronous
.Ql EVENT
lines for matching inbound Access messages.
.El
.Pp
Run
.Nm Cm help
for the full sub-verb list with argument sketches.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the daemon answered
.Ql OK ,
1 when it answered
.Ql ERR ,
and 2 on a connection or I/O error.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /var/run/meshd.sock
Default
.Xr meshd 8
control socket.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mint a network, provision a device and configure it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
meshctl create-network
meshctl provision 0102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f10 1
meshctl provision-status
meshctl cfg appkey-add 0x0005
meshctl cfg model-bind 0x0005 0x0005 0x1000
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr meshd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
